  "h1": "6 Best DataAnnotation Alternatives for AI Training Work",
  "introText": "The best DataAnnotation alternatives for remote AI training work are Outlier, Mercor, Alignerr, Mindrift, Handshake AI, and Prolific. Each platform uses a different pay model and entry standard, ranging from Mindrift's published $15 to $30 hourly entry rate to Handshake AI's $30 to $125 hourly range for graduate degree holders.\n\n Many workers look for sites like DataAnnotation when they experience empty project queues, account reviews, or want a second source of task volume.\n\nThese six platforms are evaluated using only verified records, published company pricing, legal dockets, and official worker documentation as of October 2026. Because compensation rules and project availability vary significantly by background, this guide examines how each platform handles task pricing, payout schedules, and worker vetting.",
  "rankingCriteria": "Each option is evaluated across four concrete operational factors based strictly on verified records. First, pay transparency, evaluating whether the platform publishes a clear hourly rate card or sets pay per project or task. Second, payout rails and schedules, noting whether payments arrive weekly or bi-monthly through PayPal, Stripe, direct deposit, or other processors. Third, onboarding friction and screening criteria, including educational thresholds and identity checks. Fourth, published legal and regulatory history, documenting misclassification lawsuits, Department of Labor investigations, or reported data breaches. The platforms are listed in order of how directly their workflow replaces DataAnnotation's mix of general and coding task work, rather than as a quality ranking.",
